# Official Architecture Standards

Before changing architecture or implementation, follow `docs/architecture/final-architecture.md`.

Core rules:

- Keep `src/app/page.tsx` and `src/app/layout.tsx` as Server Components.
- Use Server Components by default.
- Use Client Components only for forms, real interactivity, browser APIs, Framer Motion, GSAP, or embeds.
- Do not create global providers unless the need is truly cross-cutting.
- Keep landing sections in `src/components/sections/`.
- Keep shared UI without domain knowledge in `src/components/ui/`.
- Keep layout components in `src/components/layout/`.
- Keep helpers, schemas, loaders and services without UI in `src/lib/`.
- Keep shared hooks in `src/hooks/`; local one-off hooks can stay inside a section.
- Use `public/figma/{section}/` for Figma assets.
- Any structural decision or new long-term pattern requires an ADR.
